WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.369
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We are here with Maude Apatow.

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:04.637
You can tell,
from the audience reaction,

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:05.871
whenever I mention
the show "Euphoria,"

00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:08.408
this has
a very fervent fan base.

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:09.476
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.744
Is it fun to be
a part of something

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:13.646
that people are
paying so much attention to?

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.814
-It's so crazy.
I can't even believe it.

00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:17.917
Like, I just -- Every day,
I'm, like, on Instagram,

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.653
and people make
these super-intricate

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.523
edits and drawings,
and, like, it's so amazing.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:26.426
So, yeah, thank you, guys.
-Have you had --

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:27.993
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:27.993 --> 00:00:29.995
You know, obviously,
you have your professional life

00:00:29.995 --> 00:00:31.297
on camera.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:34.133
With your downtime,
I know that you like to --

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:37.736
and celebrate
the reality-show world.

00:00:37.736 --> 00:00:39.572
-Yes. I really do.
-Yeah.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:43.176
-You went to the
"The Bachelor" mansion.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.877
-I did go to
"The Bachelor" mansion.

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:47.580
And Colton photobombed me.
-Really?

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.882
-Like, that wasn't even inten--
He just jumped in the back.

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:51.317
I didn't even realize.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.685
-You were just taking a photo

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.220
without knowing that
Colton was there?

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.988
-But I'm so obsessed
with reality TV,

00:00:55.988 --> 00:01:00.025
I went to "The Bachelor" mansion
and sat in the control room

00:01:00.025 --> 00:01:03.029
for a rose ceremony, and it was
the coolest thing ever.

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:04.130
-Wow!
-But -- Yeah.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.532
-Is it super-tense?

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:06.833
Is there a lot of chatter
in the control room

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:07.833
during a rose ceremony?

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:09.269
-Oh, yeah, so much more.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:11.604
And I was just, like,
loving every second.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.606
It was, like, more fun to be
in the control room --

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.474
-Well, 'cause I would imagine,
in that case,

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:18.077
you've got, like, tight cameras
on, like, all the faces.

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:19.845
-Yeah.
They're talking about them,

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:21.847
and it's so --
Yeah, it was crazy.

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:23.682
But I'm a big
"90 Day Fiancé" fan.

00:01:23.682 --> 00:01:25.685
-Okay, great.
-That's my favorite.

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.553
-And do any -- Have, like --

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:30.322
Have you connected with any of
the 90-day fiancés?

00:01:30.322 --> 00:01:33.460
-This is my
most horrible trait, is, like --

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.794
So, like, the other week,
we were, like,

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:38.898
celebrating "Euphoria," and I --
I'll have like one drink,

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.467
and then I think
it's a great idea for me

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:44.804
to message the "90 Day Fiancé"
cast on Instagram.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.372
Every time. So --

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.841
-And what sort of messages
do you send them, Maude?

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:51.344
-I just hope they're okay.
-Okay.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:55.280
-Like, I just get so worried
and, like, stressed,

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.850
and I'll be watching it
and I'm, like, kind of drunk

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.420
and I'll just be like,
"Oh, no, I need to check in."

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.254
Like, I know this
was shot like -- what? --

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:03.723
four months before.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:06.693
Like, I just need to maybe check
and see how they're doing.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.361
-And do you hear back from them?

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.530
-Sometimes, but mostly not.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.698
-Okay.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:13.332
Well, they're all very busy,
and, you know,

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:14.834
they have these
new fiancés, yeah.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.169
-They know I care, so -- Yeah.

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:19.239
-I hate to put you on the spot,

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:20.506
but I'm just going to be honest.

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.475
How does that show work?

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:24.677
-"90 Day Fiancé"?
-Yeah.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:28.514
-You have, um -- Whoa!
I've -- Whoa!

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:30.316
I've been waiting
for this moment.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.817
No.

00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:34.153
-I really like
making people plug shows

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:36.088
they have nothing to do with.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:38.625
-You have one person
who's from America

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.293
and then one person
from another country.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:43.395
And the person from whatever
country they're from

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:45.831
is in America
on the spousal visa.

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:48.201
So they have
90 days to get married

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:50.436
or they have to go back to
wherever they're from.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.805
-So the show basically
puts them with a stranger.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.406
-Yes -- Or no, no, no.

00:02:54.406 --> 00:02:56.042
Sometimes,
they meet online before.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.577
-Oh, gotcha. So it's not --

00:02:57.577 --> 00:03:00.479
-Yeah, yeah. It depends.
Each situation is different.

00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:02.815
-Okay. And what percentage
is it working out on

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.016
old "90 Day Fiancé"?

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:05.150
-There are some really --

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.786
There's ones that have
really worked out.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:07.854
-Really?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:09.088
-But, like,
what percentage, Maude?

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.924
What are we talking? Like 5?

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:13.760
-Oh, my gosh.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.961
No, more than that.
More than that.

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:17.530
You have some
soul mates on there.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.232
-Really?
-Yes.

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.633
-This is wonderful to hear.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:24.737
I'm happy, because it doesn't
sound like it should work.

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:27.707
-It varies.
-Yeah.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.041
-Yeah.

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:31.377
-I've only watched --
I'm just going to come clean.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.644
I watch "Love is Blind."

00:03:32.644 --> 00:03:33.713
Have you watched
"Love is Blind"?

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:34.747
-Yes, yes.
-Yeah.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.015
-Not this season.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.716
-Yeah, there's a new season,
which my wife and I

00:03:37.716 --> 00:03:39.151
are trying to decide if
we're going to put ourselves

00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:40.653
through it again.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.355
-And they have a
"Love is Blind: Japan."

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:43.456
-Do they really?

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:44.657
-Yeah, I saw on Netflix
the other day.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:45.958
I was like, "Got to watch that."
-That's great.

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.928
I mean, it does transfer
pretty easy to other cultures.

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:50.696
I mean, I feel like
everybody understands it.

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:52.865
It's like, you're going to
fall in love by a voice.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:55.801
-Right, right.
-Like, got it. Sign up.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.069
And what about "The Bachelor"?

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:59.439
Do you feel like,
when you watch that,

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:01.807
are you mostly rooting for
true love?

00:04:01.807 --> 00:04:03.609
-I mean, of course.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:05.211
-Yeah. Okay.
-Are you?

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:08.781
-I'm kinda -- Well, alright.
-No?!

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.817
-Well, there's
a disaster element of it

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:14.420
that I feel like
makes for good TV.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.590
-But then it all, like,
is so nice when it works out.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.158
-You are --
You're built for this.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.726
You're the perfect audience.
-I'm such a sucker.

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:22.294
I'm, like, always crying.

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:23.762
They're, like, riding horses
and, like

00:04:23.762 --> 00:04:26.398
-Well, that's when I realized
I had to step back.

00:04:26.398 --> 00:04:28.367
Like, first, I had to step back
because I'm like,

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:31.671
"Oh, I'm enjoying this too much,
like, watching these people

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.439
with their
messy lives interact,"

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.274
and I felt bad about myself
as a person.

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:36.642
But then I realized
I had to step back

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:38.945
because I'm like, "Also,
I'm more invested in their love

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:41.046
than I am in any of
the friends and family

00:04:41.046 --> 00:04:44.884
and I'm fully crying about these
people that I've never met,

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:46.585
and I think
that this is unhealthy."

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:49.188
-No, I can relate to that.
That's why I message them.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.024
I care so much.

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:53.593
And, also, I always am
messaging people.

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:56.162
Like, I'll watch, like,
a random Netflix docu-series,

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:59.365
and, like, some random person
who's doing an interview --

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:01.100
I'll find them on Instagram
and be like,

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.902
"Hope everything's
going alright."

00:05:03.902 --> 00:05:06.104
-By the way, I just want to
celebrate the fact that

00:05:06.104 --> 00:05:08.774
I think I've never met anyone
who uses social media

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:10.442
just to, like,
check in on people.

00:05:10.442 --> 00:05:14.080
-No, like, my, like,
"You up?" text is, like,

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.517
sliding into a "90 Day Fiancé"
cast member's DMs,

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:20.252
asking if everything's okay.

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:21.520
-It's really great.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.656
I like to think that the
"90 Day Fiancé" --

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:24.690
when they have
their reunion thing,

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:25.991
they just talk about you.

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:27.393
They're like, "Are you getting
these weird texts?"

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.895
-This weird girl. Yeah.

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:31.297
-"You know this girl from
'Euphoria'?

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:33.065
Is she asking you
if you're okay all the time?"

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:36.235
It's like, "Yeah, we should ask
her if she's okay."

00:05:38.503 --> 00:05:40.706
-Oh, God,
that's so embarrassing.

00:05:40.706 --> 00:05:42.208
I'm like,
"Darcey, if you see this --

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:43.910
I always text her, "I love you."

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.178
-Oh, that's great.

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:48.381
Darcey, if you see this,
I think the love is real.

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:50.516
And I think you should
stop ignoring it.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:52.551
Whatever you're looking out
there for in 90 days

00:05:52.551 --> 00:05:55.254
is sitting right in this chair.

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:57.490
Hey, Maude, thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:58.524
-Thank you!

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.059
-It's such a delight
to have you.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.393
Maude Apatow, everybody.

00:06:01.393 --> 00:06:03.829
The season finale of "Euphoria"
airs this Sunday on HBO.

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:05.031
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

